**Reused evidence**
No prior chapter evidence was directly reused here. I treated formal executive-authority material as background only, not as integrity evidence.

**New evidence**
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Media in Bangladesh free to criticise my government: PM Hasina","publisher":"The Daily Star / UNB","publication_date":"2022-09-28","url":"https://www.thedailystar.net/news/bangladesh/news/media-bangladesh-free-criticise-my-government-pm-hasina-3130151","claim":"Hasina publicly said Bangladeshi media could say whatever they wished and that criticism remained free, while answering a question about the Digital Security Act.","locator":"lines 157-175","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous report of a direct public statement by the ruler with clear date and context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct public statement by Sheikh Hasina about her own government's media environment.","contrary_evidence":["HRW and Freedom House documented journalist arrests, self-censorship, and DSA-based pressure in the same period."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Free, fair polls held only during AL govt, PM Hasina tells BBC","publisher":"Prothom Alo / BSS","publication_date":"2022-09-19","url":"https://en.prothomalo.com/bangladesh/nr4z8ze208","claim":"Hasina said free and fair elections had only happened under Awami League rule and told the BBC to judge disappearance allegations by how true they were.","locator":"lines 40-43 and 52-57","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous report of an interview statement by the ruler, with exact quoted claims and a dated interview context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct public statement by Sheikh Hasina about elections and disappearances during her tenure.","contrary_evidence":["Freedom House and HRW described manipulated elections, pressure on critics, and unresolved disappearance allegations."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PM asks to give befitting reply to anti-Bangladesh propaganda","publisher":"BSS","publication_date":"2022-09-25","url":"https://www.bssnews.net/news-flash/84431","claim":"Hasina urged supporters to counter what she called propaganda and described critics as spreading false and fabricated information about Bangladesh and her government.","locator":"lines 44-53","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official wire report of a direct ruler statement with clear date, but the claim is self-serving and needs corroboration by contrary evidence.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct public statement by Sheikh Hasina; the claim concerns her own government and its critics.","contrary_evidence":["Independent reporting in 2022 documented the government's retaliation against critics, activists, and rights groups."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"AL government never violates human rights","publisher":"The Daily Star / BSS","publication_date":"2022-12-14","url":"https://www.thedailystar.net/news/bangladesh/news/al-government-never-violates-human-rights-3196391","claim":"Hasina said the Awami League never violates human rights and instead protects rights.","locator":"search result snippet","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct contemporaneous quotation reported in a wire summary; exact wording is recoverable from the snippet, though not from an open page fetch.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Direct public statement by Sheikh Hasina about her own party's conduct.","contrary_evidence":["HRW, Freedom House, and UN-related reporting in 2022 documented arbitrary arrests, repression, and impunity."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Govt scraps Odhikar’s registration","publisher":"The Daily Star","publication_date":"2022-06-06","url":"https://www.thedailystar.net/news/bangladesh/news/govt-scraps-odhikars-registration-3041281","claim":"The government cancelled Odhikar's registration after the group documented disappearances and killings, and the letter said the organization spread misleading information that tarnished the state's image.","locator":"lines 185-199","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed contemporaneous reporting with a copy of the official letter and specific administrative action against a rights group.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"The action was taken by a bureau under the government led by Hasina; it directly targeted a group documenting state abuses.","contrary_evidence":["The article also notes Odhikar was one of the few groups systematically logging disappearances, so the government's rationale is contested."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bangladesh Government Keeps Rewarding Rights Abusers","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-10-05","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/10/05/bangladesh-government-keeps-rewarding-rights-abusers","claim":"HRW reported that Hasina rewarded sanctioned RAB and police officials with promotions and medals instead of accountability, and the government sent one sanctioned police chief to a UN event to bypass a US travel ban.","locator":"lines 605-612","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed contemporaneous NGO reporting that ties the action to named sanctioned officials and to Hasina's own awards and government decisions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Hasina and her government through awards, promotions, and delegation decisions involving sanctioned loyalists.","contrary_evidence":["The government claimed business as usual and reform was unnecessary, which reinforces rather than weakens the abuse pattern."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.7","7B.9","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Govt to send IGP Benazir to UN event","publisher":"The Daily Star","publication_date":"2022-08-07","url":"https://www.thedailystar.net/news/bangladesh/news/govt-send-igp-benazir-un-event-3089331","claim":"Bangladesh decided to send police chief Benazir Ahmed to a UN summit even though the US had sanctioned him for human-rights violations.","locator":"lines 154-155 and 163-169","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific, dated report of an official government decision involving a sanctioned official and public funds.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Government action under Hasina's cabinet; it shows tolerance and validation of a sanctioned loyalist.","contrary_evidence":["The article itself notes the US sanctions and the government's effort to work around them, which cuts against any claim of accountability."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.7","7B.9","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bangladesh: Freedom in the World 2022 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/bangladesh/freedom-world/2022","claim":"Freedom House said unqualified Awami League loyalists were alleged to be getting court positions, and that cases against ruling-party activists were regularly withdrawn for 'political consideration'.","locator":"lines 212-217","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Established country report with explicit claims about judicial politicization and preferential treatment for ruling-party actors.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"country-year 2022 context with ruler nexus","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant: it describes patronage and impunity patterns under the AL government led by Hasina, not a single personal act.","contrary_evidence":["These are allegations and structural observations rather than a direct finding of Hasina's personal intent in one discrete case."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.7","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Report 2022: Bangladesh","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-01-13","url":"https://www.hrw.org/world-report/2022/country-chapters/bangladesh","claim":"HRW said the government used the Digital Security Act to harass and detain critics, targeted family members of diaspora journalists, denied disappearance findings, and reacted to spyware allegations by offering a peacekeeping explanation the UN rejected.","locator":"lines 85-90 and 126-130","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Annual country report with multiple specific mechanisms of concealment, retaliation, and official denial tied to Hasina's government.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022, with 2021-22 carryover","ruler_attribution":"The abuses are attributed to the Awami League-led government under Hasina; the report also records official denial and an implausible cover explanation from security officials.","contrary_evidence":["The government's denials and the UN's rejection of the equipment explanation are themselves evidence against candor."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bangladesh appoints Abdur Rouf Talukder as central bank governor","publisher":"bdnews24.com","publication_date":"2022-06-11","url":"https://bdnews24.com/bangladesh/bangladesh-appoints-abdur-rouf-talukder-as-central-bank-governor","claim":"The government appointed career finance secretary Abdur Rouf Talukder, who had decades of public-finance experience, as Bangladesh Bank governor.","locator":"lines 141-149","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Clear, dated appointment notice with a professional biography and no apparent controversy in the appointment itself.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"target-period 2022","ruler_attribution":"Hasina's government made the appointment; this is a modest positive counterexample to a pure-cronyism narrative.","contrary_evidence":["A single professional appointment does not show broader independence or honesty across the government."],"lenses":["7B.5"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"ACC probes land allocation allegations involving Sheikh Hasina, family","publisher":"Dhaka Tribune","publication_date":"2024-12-26","url":"https://www.dhakatribune.com/bangladesh/corruption/369177/acc-probes-land-allocation-allegations-involving","claim":"The Anti-Corruption Commission opened a probe alleging that Hasina, during her tenure as prime minister, misused authority to allocate six government plots to herself and close family members.","locator":"lines 135-155","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Later but specific investigative reporting tied to an official probe, with direct allegations about family benefit and misuse of authority.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"retrospective about conduct during Hasina's tenure; not a discrete 2022 event","ruler_attribution":"Strong family/office nexus: the allegations describe personal benefit to Hasina and relatives through government land allocation while she was in office.","contrary_evidence":["This is an allegation/probe, not a final judicial finding, so it should be treated cautiously."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.9"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I considered roughly 30 documents across The Daily Star, Prothom Alo, BSS, bdnews24, Freedom House, HRW, Dhaka Tribune, Al Jazeera, Reuters-related archive material, and later ACC/OCCRP-style graft reporting.

Accepted because they directly showed ruler statements, denial, retaliation, loyalty-based protection, or family-benefit allegations:
- The 2022 media-freedom quote, BBC interview quote, and anti-propaganda statement.
- Odhikar deregistration.
- HRW's 2022 report on rewarding sanctioned officials.
- The 2022 Benazir UN-trip report.
- Freedom House's 2022 judiciary-politicization and patronage findings.
- HRW's 2022 country report on DSA repression, family targeting, and spyware concealment.
- The 2022 central-bank-governor appointment as a modest positive counterexample.
- The 2024 ACC probe into Hasina-family land allocations as retrospective evidence of office-to-family benefit.

Removed or downgraded:
- Multiple duplicate versions of the same media-freedom, human-rights, and protest-repression stories from different outlets.
- Generic corruption indices and country-level rule-of-law scores, which were treated as context only and not as personal-integrity evidence.
- Later 2025/2026 verdict stories and some post-ouster commentary, because they were beyond the target year and were not needed once the 2022 and retrospective 2024 probe material was in hand.
- Broad human-rights summaries that did not add a ruler-specific personal nexus beyond sources already accepted.

**Remaining gaps**
- Direct 2022 asset-disclosure, beneficial-ownership, bank, or procurement records tied personally to Hasina or immediate family.
- More direct evidence of Hasina personally correcting false claims rather than doubling down.
- Stronger 2022 documentation of private enrichment or business conflicts, rather than later allegations/probes.
- Clearer proof of personal instruction versus subordinate action on retaliation and patronage.

More search would help, mainly on 7B.3, 7B.4, and 7B.8.
